/Dest [ 416 0 R /Fit ] /Next 504 0 R /Parent 497 0 R /Prev 502 0 R /Title (Q5. A village repaired its pond before drilling new borewells. The pond did not create rain, but it slowed runoff and allowed more water to seep underground. Wells nearby recovered sooner after the monsoon than wells farther away. The result supports recharge as one part of water security, not as a substitute for demand management.)
>>
